/-!
# RT_FB on 8 placer seeds of the routed 64-stage Muller pipeline (probe C-10f)

Data: seed 1 is 10d's `RoutedMuller64S1`; seeds 2..8 are `RtFbM64S2..8`, generated by
`formal/tools/rtfb/muller_rt.sh` (10d's `rt_all.py`, unchanged, on 11b's `fasm2lean`
read-back of each seed's bitstream; nextpnr 9c732bc6303458df, cells/flow.sh options,
`--freq 100 --seed s`, fasm_audit PASS).  RT_FB(i) and the interval variants are 10d's
(see `RoutedMuller.lean`): `indep` = H_INDEP, `fast`/`slow` = H_ONE_CORNER with RC in
[0, E], `fastE`/`slowE` = H_ONE_CORNER + H_RC_EXACT, `sdf` = nextpnr's numbers (not a bound).

Kernel-checked (`decide +kernel`, no native code): per seed and variant, the number of
C-elements that PASS RT_FB (`m64sN_pass`), and the worst slack over all 64 C-elements
(`m64sN_worst`).  Every passing entry is proved for all runs (`rt_sound_of`) and every
failing entry has a violating fixed-delay run (`rt_violated_of`), so each count is exact
in its model (side conditions `m64sN_wf`, `m64sN_sep`).

| seed | indep | fast | slow | fastE | slowE | sdf |  (failing of 64)
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 42 | 16 | 14 | 12 | 12 | 1 |
| 2 | 43 | 11 | 8 | 4 | 5 | 0 |
| 3 | 41 | 14 | 14 | 11 | 11 | 0 |
| 4 | 39 | 9 | 7 | 5 | 5 | 0 |
| 5 | 37 | 7 | 6 | 4 | 4 | 0 |
| 6 | 43 | 12 | 8 | 4 | 4 | 0 |
| 7 | 40 | 11 | 10 | 7 | 7 | 0 |
| 8 | 42 | 15 | 15 | 11 | 10 | 0 |
-/

namespace Formal.Timing.RtFb
